  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Circular Textile Hack 2.0</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to expand the Textile Hack at BUFT through an online platform for challenge-based, application-oriented learning integrated into the existing curriculum. Through this platform, a hybrid, credit-bearing course will be developed, combining online modules with offline, student-led activities and direct engagement with the RMG private sector, with external visibility provided through various online channels and an offline Prototype Bazar showcasing the most promising student outcomes. Building on the K2K textile and circular economy hackathon programme, the project aims to strengthen practical entrepreneurship education and teaching capacity, while increasing awareness and applied understanding of circular and sustainable supply chains, with support from Dutch academia.</narrative>
  </description>
